course: dictionary
lesson: 182
title: Aid: help and helpers
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Aid means help. It can be help given to people who need it, such as food, water or money, or a thing that helps you, such as a hearing aid. «First aid is the help you give someone straight away, before a doctor comes.» Here, first aid is help given at once.
explain: Look at the words around aid to find its meaning. A first aid kit holds plasters and bandages, so the kit is full of things that help when someone is hurt. The clues tell you that aid is something useful that helps people.
explain: Aid can also be a verb. To aid someone means to help them. Try the swap check: put help in place of aid in the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Aid means help, especially money, food or care for people who need it.
fact: An aid is a thing that helps you, like a hearing aid.
fact: To aid someone means to help them.
fact: «First aid» means the simple help you give someone who is hurt, before a doctor comes.
fact: «Come to someone's aid» means to help them.
exercise: «First aid is the help you give someone straight away, before a doctor comes.» What is first aid? | A type of school uniform | A long stay in hospital for a doctor | *The simple help you give someone who is hurt, before a doctor comes | A game played at break time
exercise: Grandad wears a hearing aid. What is a hearing aid? | A loud noise made by a radio | A quiet room for reading | A kind of hearing test that is never used | *A thing that helps a person hear better
exercise: «Countries send aid, like food, water and medicine, after a flood.» What does aid mean here? | A kind of rain | A map of the river | Clothes for a holiday | *Help, such as food, water and medicine
test: «Ruby ran to aid her friend when he fell off his bike.» What does aid mean here? | To shout at | *To help | To hurt | To stop
test: «A first aid kit holds plasters and bandages.» What does a first aid kit hold? | A bag of sweets | A fishing rod | *Plasters and bandages | A box of toys
exam: «The charity will aid the families who lost their homes.» What does aid mean in this sentence? | To move away | *To help | To ignore | To pay a fine
